/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (General elections were held in India from 19 April to 1 June 2024 in seven phases, to elect all 543 members of the Lok Sabha. On 7 June 2024, Shri Narendra Modi confirmed the support of 293 MPs to Smt. Droupadi Murmu, the Hon'ble president of India and this marked Modi's third term as Prime Minister and his first time heading a coalition government\(NDA\). The primary opposition was the Indian National Developmental Inclusive Alliance\(INDIA\), a coalition formed by the Indian National Congress \(INC\) and many regional parties in 2023. )
/E (General elections were held in India from 19 April to 1 June 2024 in seven phases, to elect all 543 members of the Lok Sabha. On 7 June 2024, Shri Narendra Modi confirmed the support of 293 MPs to Smt. Droupadi Murmu, the Hon'ble president of India and this marked Modi's third term as Prime Minister and his first time heading a coalition government\(NDA\). The primary opposition was the Indian National Developmental Inclusive Alliance\(INDIA\), a coalition formed by the Indian National Congress \(INC\) and many regional parties in 2023. )
