250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Soon, they discover that they have been brought together by a mysterious host who accuses each of them of past crimes and begins to exact his own form of justice. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( The story begins with each character receiving an invitation to Soldier Island, a remote location off the coast of Devon, England. Upon arrival, they find themselves isolated from the mainland and without any way to leave. The tension mounts as, during dinner, a gramophone recording accuses each guest of committing murder and escaping justice. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The guests are shocked and deny the accusations, however the atmosphere of mistrust and fear slowly but surely begins to grow. The guests soon discover a sinister nursery rhyme displayed in each room. The rhyme becomes a chilling countdown, predicting the fate of each character.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
