/ActualText <>
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The idea of war has never been alien to humans. Ever since the evolution of mankind, and as far back as history goes, wars have always been waged - for security, for revenge, to assert dominance, or in the name of religion.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Protolithic humans fought with stones. Stones evolved into swords and arrows. Swords and arrows turned into guns and cannons. Guns and cannons shifted to missiles. Missiles gave way to nuclear weapons - for the sake of destruction, no ruin is enough havoc.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
